# Punctuation: no dashes, spare semicolons

Applies to assistant chat replies and to prose written into project content (notes, questionnaires, docs, spreadsheet cells). Does not change code operators, URLs, file paths, or markdown list markers (`-` / `*`).

## Dashes

- Never use em dashes (—) or en dashes (–).
- Do not use a hyphen as a sentence break or aside (e.g. rewrite "Yes - Coach Create" as "Yes. Coach Create").
- Prefer periods, commas, colons, or separate sentences.
- Normal compound words that need a hyphen (e.g. `30-day`, `well-known`) are fine when that is standard English spelling.

```
❌ Yes — Coach Create supports monogram.
❌ Yes - Coach Create supports monogram.
✅ Yes. Coach Create supports monogram.
```

## Semicolons

- Highly discouraged in prose.
- Prefer a period and a new sentence, or a comma / bullet list when listing items.

```
❌ Size on apparel; colors often separate PDPs.
✅ Size on apparel. Colors often separate PDPs.
✅ Size on apparel
✅ Colors often separate PDPs
```
